{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475703-what-s-up-with-elixir","id":1475703,"title":"What's up with Elixir?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-02T20:40:07-08:00","id":1475703,"title":"What's up with Elixir?","content":"There's a small rule in the writeup on the Elixir Endowment that I find puzzling: that an Ascending hunter may only possess up to her Stamina + Elixir rating in them at one time. It's not clear to me why one's haleness has any bearing on the number of magic drugs one can lug around. I can see from a certain design perspective why one might want to place an artificial cap in order to abjure the siren song of industrialism, though all the same I wonder if this should have been handled as a social problem instead. I'm reminded of similar dissonance with the Alchemist class in Pathfinder, though there at least one finds the (very flimsy) justification of a magic spark that must be diffused among potions. I wish to be as uncritical as possible here; the rule survived three drafts so obviously the devs thought it was important to keep, though I'll also note that the Endowment already comes with multiple drawbacks (Willpower costs, dice rolls, near-omnipresent Backlash), so I'm a little uncertain as to the ultimate guiding principle. Any insight would be appreciated. (Any tips with a midwest hookup for Incense of the Next World would also be appreciated.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T20:56:28-08:00","id":1475704,"title":"","content":"Maybe the elixirs themselves, their containers, and any tools needed to imbibe them properly, are deceptively heavy and unwieldy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T21:11:13-08:00","id":1475705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475703-what-s-up-with-elixir?p=1475704#post1475704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the elixirs themselves, their containers, and any tools needed to imbibe them properly, are deceptively heavy and unwieldy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but what if one leaves a few draughts behind in the safehouse? Are these also constrained by the limit? It's mysterious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T21:11:55-08:00","id":1475706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475703-what-s-up-with-elixir#post1475703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a small rule in the writeup on the Elixir Endowment that I find puzzling: that an Ascending hunter may only possess up to her Stamina + Elixir rating in them at one time. It's not clear to me why one's haleness has any bearing on the number of magic drugs one can lug around.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording is &quot;hold as many prepared elixirs on her person,&quot; which is not quite in the spirit of &quot;lugging them around.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're magic drugs cut with poison. The number of places you can keep them on you close at hand enough to use them as an instant action is limited, and becomes less so as your training in their use advances and your natural resistance to normal drugs and poisons increases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T21:15:11-08:00","id":1475707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475703-what-s-up-with-elixir?p=1475705#post1475705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but what if one leaves a few draughts behind in the safehouse? Are these also constrained by the limit? It's mysterious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn\u2019t that limit in place for the elixirs you carry on your person specifically? So the ones in a safehouse would be exempt, iirc (not sure; not with the book atm)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T07:26:47-08:00","id":1475731,"title":"","content":"Notice the emphasize on Stamina as part of the limit- the AO are alchemists which use their own body as a furnace in order to transform poison into power through faith. At least half of the process of their alchemy is internal. The limit is best rationalized, IMO, as the hunter not only preparing the ingredients and potions, but also refining their body for those elixirs they prepared. Kinda like how a wizard is preparing spells in d&amp;d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T09:00:36-08:00","id":1475737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475703-what-s-up-with-elixir?p=1475731#post1475731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice the emphasize on Stamina as part of the limit- the AO are alchemists which use their own body as a furnace in order to transform poison into power through faith. At least half of the process of their alchemy is internal. The limit is best rationalized, IMO, as the hunter not only preparing the ingredients and potions, but also refining their body for those elixirs they prepared. Kinda like how a wizard is preparing spells in d&amp;d.</div> </div> </div> </div>THis is probably the most accurate way to think about it. adjoined with the fact that, while reasonably anyone can make Elixers in AO as a result of training to use them, it decently follows due ot the rarity of a lot of the ingredients that a lot of it gets distributed from the Order of the Southern Temple through the Jagged Crescent to everyone else, and as such the two together can reasonably form a pipeline of consideration for &quot;Hey, this stuff CAN kill you, maybe you want a second opinion before getting it.&quot;<br /> <br /> AO's structure is , of course, very loose, and has a lot of cell independence, so it can be fudged-but it's not exactly lacking in a community control element either.<br /> <br /> But mostly, it's a &quot;reach within grasp&quot; sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-03-2022, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T19:19:46-08:00","id":1475870,"title":"","content":"I see. So it is primarily a social issue for an Ascending One, then (insofar as the temples verify one's skill before they okay the distribution of Elixirs). I kind of wonder if this could have better been represented with, say, Status + Elixir, though the calculation as-is does overlap perfectly with the dice pool for using the Endowment.<br /> <br /> In light of the sidebar in their writeup, I wonder if the Conspiracy has had issues with members hoarding Elixirs in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T20:15:06-08:00","id":1475873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475703-what-s-up-with-elixir?p=1475870#post1475870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. So it is primarily a social issue for an Ascending One, then (insofar as the temples verify one's skill before they okay the distribution of Elixirs). I kind of wonder if this could have better been represented with, say, Status + Elixir, though the calculation as-is does overlap perfectly with the dice pool for using the Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>In First Edition, you started with [Elixirs + Status: Ascending Ones] dots' worth of Elixirs, started each new story with [Elixirs] dots' worth of Elixirs, and had to spend days of time and experience points (Practical or otherwise) recovering them as single-use items through brewing or requisition. Second Edition cuts that down to an hour and free, swapping out the recovery cost for the need to buy new dots/recipes, and the different Elixirs are no longer granularly rated and thus can't be spread out as &quot;ten dots' worth of potions, whether that's two five-dots or ten one-dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again: Magic drugs cut with poison, made with exotic ingredients and alchemical knowledge. These are not used freely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:13:49-08:00","id":1476104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475703-what-s-up-with-elixir?p=1475873#post1475873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In First Edition, you started with [Elixirs + Status: Ascending Ones] dots' worth of Elixirs, started each new story with [Elixirs] dots' worth of Elixirs, and had to spend days of time and experience points (Practical or otherwise) recovering them as single-use items through brewing or requisition. Second Edition cuts that down to an hour and free, swapping out the recovery cost for the need to buy new dots/recipes, and the different Elixirs are no longer granularly rated and thus can't be spread out as &quot;ten dots' worth of potions, whether that's two five-dots or ten one-dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again: Magic drugs cut with poison, made with exotic ingredients and alchemical knowledge. These are not used freely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been a while since I read First Edition, forgot that's how it worked back then. You know, reading back over the text, I think my brain filled in a part that isn't actually there about the Temples providing hunters with the Elixirs themselves, rather than simply the ingredients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}